Dear OSY & list:


There are a number of configurations of the storageworks boxes.  The
box internal bus is single-ended, so it doesn't work well on the same
bus with differential devices.  There is a way to share a bus between
the BA box and diffferential devices, but you need the personality
module with 2 sets of switches.  The 4-switch unit allows you to turn
off termination, then you use a Y-cable and external terminator, plus
a jumper unit that goes in the box.

This sounds like a lot of work, and the parts could be a little hard
to get.  Another solution is to run your BA box off its own Qlogic
card.  The Qlogic 1040 is single-ended and works OK with the BA box. 
You can test your card and box combo by unhooking the internal drive
cable, connecting the BA box and going into your SRM -  you should get
a decent report from "sh dev".


good luck

jn

