I'm not sure I understand the question.
You can't get into AlphaBIOS (if your boxes run NT, then you've got
AlphaBIOS)? iirc, it's just like on PC BIOS'es, showing you something 
like "Press DEL to enter setup" on startup.
Reflashing it to srm is just a matter of fetching the right ROM from
ftp.digital.com, putting it on a FAT floppy and pressing "Upgrade bios"
in AlphaBIOS (on LXes. Other boards may have both srm and AlphaBIOS in
rom, then switching is done from the BIOS itself).

