Actually I solved it!

  That's a very good point but it turns out one ribbon equals one interface.

  In the kernel source in ide-pci.c it uses the constant MAX_HWIFS
which I assumed(!) was 10. I put in a printk and it's 4!

  I knew this was defined in a .h somewhere but where? I got frustrated 
and went into include/ in the kernel source three and did a brute-force 
search of different wildcard depths till I got:

grep MAX_HWIFS */* | grep -i define

Here is what I got! Pretty logical place for it, really!

asm-alpha/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS       4
asm-arm/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS 4
asm-cris/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        4
asm-i386/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        10
asm-i386/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        6
asm-ia64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        10
asm-ia64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        6
asm-m68k/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        4       /* same as the other 
archs */
asm-mips64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS      10
asm-mips64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS      6
asm-mips/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        10
asm-mips/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        6
asm-parisc/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS      2
asm-ppc64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS       4
asm-ppc/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS 8
asm-s390/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS        0
asm-s390x/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS       0
asm-sh/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS  2
asm-sparc64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS     2
asm-sparc/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS       2
asm-x86_64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS      10
asm-x86_64/ide.h:#define MAX_HWIFS      6

Who knows why they did that, I guess they didn't expect autoprobed 
interfaces on alpha. I changed it to a 6 and recompiled. Six drives on 
six different ribbons, everything works!! Yay! I have no idea how high 
you can actually go. No intention of finding out either!

Now I have to do some testing to make sure this is reliable and stable, 
but so far it looks pretty good and the speed of this box is pretty 
respectable for a six year old machine! So far, it does what I want. 
I'll just back things up as best I can until I completely trust it. It's 
all my data....

Now I can get some sleep....

Thanks,
=Rich
_____________________________________________________________________
Richard Mortimer Humphrey
CCRMA

