> The simple answer is that ATA133 will
> not work.

This once again depens on SRM.  My Nautilus board boot just fine from
ATA (although I do not remember now a top speed).  On older boards
a support for IDE can vary from dismal to laughable.  Still such
sweeping statements are a bit too broad.

