Your BA356 should have what they call a "personality module", it is
part of the removable unit where the SCSI cable plugs in.  There are
different personality modules, each one does something a little
different.  Take yours out and look for two sets of jumpers .. these
have to be set correctly or else your SCSI controller has fits and
nothing works right.  Look in the following for the jumper settings:

http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/cluster_doc/cluster_15/TCR_HWCFG/CHSCSRQX.HTM#sec-ba35x-termination

I have used my BA356 with both the Qlogic PCI card and an Adaptec
3940, with good results, but only after setting the jumpers as
outlined by the above site.  BTW i just bought 5 9G U2W drives on eBay
for $140. My plan is to get a DEC raid controller and set up the BA356
as a RAID. Maybe buy another one too as they are cheap and will work
fine up to SCSI 3

good luck

