executable.  If you compile source code yourself, you must respect the
IEEE 80-bit long_precision requirement (the full bandwidth of the
Intel math coprocessor).  Microsoft C++ compilers do not go beyond
64-bit (they lie if they say otherwise), and that is not good enough.

You will be calculating the handedness (parity divergence) of balls of
single crystal tellurium between 100,000 A and 204,000 A radius, or
123 trillion to one quadrillion atoms.  This will extend

http://www.mazepath.com/uncleal/chite2.png

1/3 of a log unit in radius.  It doesn't sound like much, but it is! 
Oh yes indeedy!  CHI is like infinity - it gets exciting toward the
high end.  You get a citation in the scholarly paper, if and when. 
