" DiskMan" <nobody@thewheel.com> writes:

> I was wondering, whats the difference between "-mcpu=pca56"  and "-arch
> pca56"? Is there any difference or is it two different ways to do the same
> thing?

There isn't a -march flag for Alpha.  However, there is a -mtune flag.
Its effect is to schedule the instructions for optimal execution on
the given cpu type.  The instruction set used is not changed.  Setting
-mcpu will choose the best instruction set available on the Alpha
variant chosen, and also schedule for that cpu, unless -mtune is also
specified.

