for the hydrocarbon twistane, C(10)H(16).  Twistane is you average
boring lump of wax, except it has an optical rotation of 414 degrees. 
A commonplace chiral hydrocarbon would have an optical rotation of
about 1 degree under the same circumstances.  Big CHI values portend
interesting properties.

