>>port on the motherboard that is connected a SCSI CD-ROM. All the hard
>>drives are in removeable hard drive covers. Any ideas?
>
>Sounds like one of the drives has the same ID as the controller;
>check your jumpers.

SCSI IDs are assigned to StorageWorks slots, and the disk drive gets
the ID of the slot it is inserted into.  Move one of the drives to
another slot.  Maybe take all the Storageworks cartridges out, and
then insert them one at a time, checking for SCSI IDs.

    carl

